1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,767
Thinking about a tankless water heater to save money?

2
00:00:02,887 --> 00:00:06,459
If yours runs on electricity, look at these numbers first.

3
00:00:06,579 --> 00:00:12,491
Under federal rules, a standard fifty-gallon electric tank is rated at about point nine two.

4
00:00:12,611 --> 00:00:15,516
An electric tankless heater, about point nine one.

5
00:00:15,636 --> 00:00:16,983
That's basically the same.

6
00:00:17,103 --> 00:00:25,107
So the yearly cost barely moves: about four hundred ninety-two dollars with the tank, and about four hundred ninety-eight tankless.

7
00:00:25,227 --> 00:00:27,788
The real upgrade is a heat pump water heater.

8
00:00:27,908 --> 00:00:33,886
ENERGY STAR models are rated at least three point three, about three point six times as efficient.

9
00:00:34,006 --> 00:00:36,445
That's about a hundred thirty-seven dollars a year,

10
00:00:36,565 --> 00:00:39,150
roughly three hundred fifty-five dollars saved.

11
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:43,914
So if you're thinking about tankless to save money, and your water heater is electric…
